      "message": "[KERNELS] Accelerate Blackwell and Hopper layout conversions (#11565)\n\n## Summary\n\nLayout conversion can require repeated padding, transposes, repacking,\nand full-tensor copies. This PR converts directly into the destination\nwith Triton kernels, accelerating Blackwell value/scale conversions and\nHopper scale conversions while preserving padding, strides, and fallback\nbehavior. Scale kernels use byte views to support FNUZ FP8 storage\nwithout requiring hardware arithmetic support for those formats.\nOrdinary FakeTensors retain the Torch fallback; explicit compile warmup\ncaptures the same conversion specializations used at runtime through\nshared state that does not initialize CUDA during import. Ragged inverse\nconversion zeros unused logical capacity, including when there are no\nslices.\n\nAll timings below clear L2 before **every sample** by writing zeros\nacross a separate buffer: 1 GiB on GB300 (129.25 MiB L2), 512 MiB on\nH100 (50 MiB L2). CUDA-graph event pairs bracket only the conversion;\ncache clearing and CPU allocation/launch overhead are excluded. Results\nare the median of three trials of 32 samples each; API tables use\npreallocated output. Bandwidth counts required input + output bytes.\n`rhs` uses K-axis `-2`; `lhs` uses K-axis `-1`.\n\n### Blackwell — GB300\n\nBaseline: `main` at `7ff97e310935`. Peak bandwidth: [8 TB/s per\nGPU](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/data-center/gb300-nvl72/).\n\n| From | To | Logical shape | Main (ms) | PR (ms) | Speedup | PR TB/s |\nMain → PR % peak |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `Strided(rhs)`<br>(K-Packed) | `ValueLayout`<br>(K-Packed) | 64 × 4096\n× 8192 | 0.706528 | 0.311296 | 2.27× | 6.899 | 38.0% → 86.2% |\n| `ValueLayout`<br>(K-Packed) | `Strided(rhs)`<br>(K-Packed) | 64 × 4096\n× 8192 | 0.706560 | 0.311296 | 2.27× | 6.899 | 38.0% → 86.2% |\n| `Strided(rhs)`<br>(K-Packed) | `ValueShuffledLayout`<br>(K-Packed) |\n64 × 4096 × 8192 | 0.309248 | 0.309248 | 1.00× | 6.944 | 86.8% → 86.8% |\n| `ValueShuffledLayout`<br>(K-Packed) | `Strided(rhs)`<br>(K-Packed) |\n64 × 4096 × 8192 | 0.313072 | 0.312480 | 1.00× | 6.872 | 85.7% → 85.9% |\n| `Strided(lhs)` | `ActScaleLayout` | 64 × 8192 × 256 | 0.485008 |\n0.045056 | 10.76× | 5.958 | 6.9% → 74.5% |\n| `ActScaleLayout` | `Strided(lhs)` | 64 × 8192 × 256 | 0.388832 |\n0.044880 | 8.66× | 5.981 | 8.6% → 74.8% |\n| `Strided(rhs)` | `ScaleLayout` | 64 × 256 × 8192 | 0.554656 | 0.045056\n| 12.31× | 5.958 | 6.0% → 74.5% |\n| `ScaleLayout` | `Strided(rhs)` | 64 × 256 × 8192 | 1.306624 | 0.045056\n| 29.00× | 5.958 | 2.6% → 74.5% |\n| `Strided(lhs)` | `ActScaleLayout`<br>(Ragged) | 524288 × 256 |\n0.592560 | 0.047072 | 12.59× | 5.735 | 5.7% → 71.7% |\n| `ActScaleLayout`<br>(Ragged) | `Strided(lhs)` | 524288 × 256 |\n0.538272 | 0.046784 | 11.51× | 5.727 | 6.2% → 71.6% |\n\n### Hopper — H100\n\nBaseline: `49babf9669a2`, before fused Hopper scale conversion. Peak\nbandwidth: [3.35 TB/s](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/data-center/h100/).\n“Layout warps” selects the scale encoding for a 4- or 8-warp matmul.\n\n| From | To | Scale shape | Layout warps | Baseline (ms) | PR (ms) |\nSpeedup | PR TB/s | Baseline → PR % peak |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `Strided(rhs)` | `HopperScaleLayout` | 16 × 128 × 3072 | 4 | 0.110592\n| 0.010112 | 10.94× | 1.244 | 3.4% → 37.1% |\n| `HopperScaleLayout` | `Strided(rhs)` | 16 × 128 × 3072 | 4 | 0.153888\n| 0.010752 | 14.31× | 1.170 | 2.4% → 34.9% |\n| `Strided(rhs)` | `HopperScaleLayout` | 16 × 128 × 3072 | 8 | 0.110272\n| 0.010160 | 10.85× | 1.238 | 3.4% → 37.0% |\n| `HopperScaleLayout` | `Strided(rhs)` | 16 × 128 × 3072 | 8 | 0.153008\n| 0.010928 | 14.00× | 1.151 | 2.5% → 34.4% |\n| `Strided(rhs)` | `HopperScaleLayout` | 64 × 256 × 8192 | 4 | 2.337072\n| 0.099360 | 23.52× | 2.702 | 3.4% → 80.6% |\n| `HopperScaleLayout` | `Strided(rhs)` | 64 × 256 × 8192 | 4 | 3.450512\n| 0.096816 | 35.64× | 2.773 | 2.3% → 82.8% |\n| `Strided(rhs)` 